+	pm_runtime_get_sync(dev);
+	pm_runtime_put_noidle(dev);
+	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
+	if (irq)
+		free_irq(mpu3050->irq, mpu3050->trig);
+	iio_triggered_buffer_cleanup(indio_dev);
```
and in remove:
```
+	iio_device_unregister(indio_dev);
```
Reason:
The fix moves `iio_device_register()` to the end of the probe function, after all initialization steps (trigger probe, runtime PM setup) are completed. This ensures the device is only exposed to userspace when all resources are ready. The error path (`err_iio_device_register`) now correctly tears down runtime PM and the trigger before the buffer cleanup, preventing leaks. In the remove function, `iio_device_unregister()` is called before tearing down resources (PM, trigger, buffer) to ensure no userspace accesses occur during teardown.

